20. FIREBASE SECURITY
==================================================

Implement secure Firestore Security Rules.

Requirements:

1. Public visitors can read active products and categories.
2. Only administrators can create, edit or remove products.
3. Customers can access their own profiles.
4. Customers can access their own carts.
5. Customers can access their own wishlists.
6. Customers can read only their own orders.
7. Customers cannot modify order totals or payment statuses.
8. Customers cannot change their administrator permissions.
9. Administrative operations must be authorized on the backend.
10. Never expose service account credentials or private API keys in frontend code.

Do not use permissive rules such as:

allow read, write: if true;

Use default-deny security rules.

Generate the security rules and explain which parts require administrative privileges.

Before deployment, test all security-sensitive operations.

